.Dd June 14, 2026
.Dt TEST 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm test
.Nd API for writing tests
.Sh LIBRARY
.Lb libtest
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In test.h
.Vt "typedef void *" test_case_state_t ;
.Vt "typedef bool" test_case_setup_function_t Ns Pq test_case_state_t *state ;
.Vt "typedef bool" test_case_teardown_function_t Ns Pq test_case_state_t state ;
.Vt "typedef void" test_function_t Ns Pq test_case_state state ;
.Ft void
.Fn test_result "enum test_result result"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Lb libtest
library implements an API for writing tests intended to be used
with the
.Xr test_driver 3
API.
.Ss Test Functions
Tests are implemented using
.Sq test functions
of type
.Vt test_function_t .
A test function verifies one (or more) assertions about the behavior
of the software it is meant to test.
The mapping between the set of assertions covering the behavior of the
system under test and the test functions in a test suite is described
by
.Xr test 5 .
.Pp
A test function communicates a test result to the test driver
by calling
.Xr test_result 3 .
A test function needs to call
.Xr test_result 3
at least once prior to returning to its caller.
The supported values for the argument
.Ar result
are:
.Bl -tag -width "Bq Dv TEST_UNRESOLVED"
.It Dv TEST_PASS
All of the assertions tested by the test function were true.
.It Dv TEST_FAIL
At least one of the assertions tested by the test function was false.
.It Dv TEST_UNRESOLVED
The test function could not meaningfully proceed for some reason.
It is not known whether the assertions tested by the test function are
true or false.
.El
.Ss Setup and Teardown Functions
Test functions can optionally be associated with a
.Sq setup function
of type
.Vt test_case_setup_function_t
and a
.Sq teardown function
of type
.Vt test_case_teardown_function_t .
.Pp
If a setup function exists, it will be called prior to any of its
associated test functions.
If a teardown function exists, it will be called after its associated
test functions are called.
.Pp
A setup function allocates resources for the use of test functions,
and a teardown function releases these resources.
The setup function can return a pointer to an allocated memory arena
in the location pointed to by its argument
.Va "state" .
This pointer value is passed to test functions when they are invoked,
and to the teardown function.
The
.Lb libtest
framework treats the pointer setup by a setup function as an opaque
value.
.Pp
Setup and teardown functions return
.Dv true
to indicate that their respective operations succeeded.
If a setup function returns
.Dv false
its associated test functions will not be called and test execution
will proceed to invoking the associated teardown function if a
teardown function is present.
A teardown function can return
.Dv false
to that the resources allocated by the setup operation were not
succesfully released.
.Ss Test Cases
Related test functions may be grouped into
.Sq test cases .
The test functions in a test case share setup and teardown functions.
.Ss Test Executables
Test functions are contained in a
.Sq test executable ,
usually implemented with the scaffolding provided by
.Xr test_driver 3 .
.Ss Scaffolding Generation
The
.Xr make-test-scaffolding 1
script can be used to generate the scaffolding needed to produce a
test executable from object files containing symbols that follow its
naming conventions.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr make-test-scaffolding 1 ,
.Xr test_driver 3 ,
.Xr test 5
